;RESIDUES GLN 66, TYR 67, GLY 68 ARE MODIFIED TO MAKE                 
THE CHROMOPHORE CRQ 68.                                              
THE N OF CRQ 66 SHARES A DOUBLE BOND WITH CA1 OF                     
CRQ 68 WHICH IS SP2 HYBRIDIZED (PLANAR).  THEREFORE,                 
WHILE THE PEPTIDE BOND BETWEEN PHE 65 AND CRQ 68 MOST                
CLOSELY RESEMBLES A CIS PEPTIDE-BOND, THIS IS NOT A                  
STANDARD PEPTIDE BOND.  THERE ARE 6 RESONANCE FORMS                  
OF CRQ.
;
